{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns-require-modification","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Bound nouns cannot occur independently and must be modified by a determiner, a noun, or a relative clause.","ja":"所属名詞（結合名詞）は単独では生起できず、限定詞、名詞、または関係節による修飾を必要とする。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"obligatory","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0007-06","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2015@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0006-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-names-rarely-adnominally-modified","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Proper names are only in extremely rare cases modified by an adnoun or an adnominal clause.","ja":"固有名詞が連体詞や連体修飾節によって修飾されることは極めて稀である。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"almost-none","modality":"neutral","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-11","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0082-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--because-a-noun-phrase-consumes-one-of-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Because a noun phrase consumes one of the argument slots required by a verb, an independent noun phrase has an arity of -1.","ja":"名詞句が文中にひとつ増えると動詞が要求する名詞句の数がひとつ減るため、自立した名詞句自体のアリティは -1 である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0258-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--certain-bound-nouns-including-kur-utar-us-i","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Certain bound nouns, including kur, utar, us(i)(ke)(he), pe/p, hike, and hi/i, occur more frequently as relative clause heads than common nouns.","ja":"kur、utar、us(i)(ke)(he)、pe/p、hike、hi/i などの結合名詞は、普通名詞よりも関係節主要部として高頻度で用いられる。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kur","utar","usike","usi","pe","p","hike","hi","i"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2015@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0006-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--obligatorily-possessed-nouns-almost-never-occur-without-possessive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Obligatorily possessed nouns almost never occur without possessive morphology.","ja":"義務的所有名詞は所有形態素を伴わずに現れることがほとんどない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0011-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--ainu-uses-unspecified-possessor-and-antipassive-morphology-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu uses unspecified possessor and antipassive morphology as non-possessed noun (NPN) morphology, allowing an obligatorily possessed noun to be used without a specified possessor or an overt possessor.","ja":"アイヌ語は不特定所有者および逆受動形態論を非所有名詞形態論として用い、義務的所有名詞を特定所有者や明示的な所有者なしで使用できるようにしている。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0037-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--without-an-overt-personal-prefix-the-default-interpretation","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Without an overt personal prefix, the default interpretation of an obligatorily possessed noun is that the possessor is third person.","ja":"人称接頭辞がない場合、義務的所有名詞の所属主は三人称であるとデフォルトで解釈される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["absence of personal prefix on inalienable noun"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--ainu-inalienable-nouns-include-body-part-terms-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu inalienable nouns include body part terms and their semantic extensions, including bodily secretions, physical strength, disposition, home, and clothing.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡不能名詞には、身体部位名詞および分泌物・体力・気質・住居・衣服などのその意味的拡張が含まれる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["tek-e","kem-ihi","nupe-he","etor-o","kiror-o","kewtum-u","ramac-ihi","re-he","kur-ihi","uni-hi","mip-ihi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--the-nouns-si-and-osoma-excrement-and-okuyma","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"The nouns si and osoma 'excrement' and okuyma 'urine' are encoded as alienably possessed nouns.","ja":"si、osoma「糞」および okuyma「尿」は譲渡可能所有名詞として記号化される。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["si","osoma","okuyma"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--in-riddles-obligatorily-possessed-nouns-are-cited-with","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"In riddles, obligatorily possessed nouns are cited with the fourth-person/first-person plural inclusive transitive subject prefix a- rather than in their conceptual form.","ja":"謎々において、義務的所有名詞は概念形ではなく、一人称複数包括／四人称他動詞主語接頭辞 a- を伴う所属形で用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["in riddles"]},"forms":["a-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-noun-roots-such-as-me-cold-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Bound noun roots such as me- 'cold' and mon- 'hand' have an arity of -1 in the calculation of compound word arity, despite not being independent words.","ja":"√me「寒さ」や √mon「手」などの名詞語根は単独で単語にならないが、合成語のアリティ計算においては普通名詞と同様に -1 として扱われる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["me-","mon-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0260-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
