{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--nineteenth-century-japanese-records-preserve-names-of-ethnic","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--bound-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Nineteenth-century Japanese records preserve names of ethnic groups derived from the Ainu element -kur, meaning 'people'.","ja":"19世紀の日本語記録には、「人」を意味するアイヌ語要素 -kur に由来する民族名が現れる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-kur"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shiraishitangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0045-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--both-ordinary-nouns-and-locative-nouns-change-their","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Both ordinary nouns and locative nouns change their forms through the attachment of suffixes to their basic forms.","ja":"普通名詞と位置名詞はともに、基本形に接尾辞が付加されることによって語形が変化する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0092-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--all-ordinary-nouns-have-an-underlying-affiliative-form","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"All ordinary nouns have an underlying affiliative form that surfaces when semantic conditions such as a material-product relationship are met.","ja":"すべての普通名詞は基底において所属形を持つ性質があり、材料と製品の関係などの意味条件が満たされれば表面化する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["when semantic conditions are met"]},"forms":["cise-he"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0093-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
