{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--the-conceptual-form-of-ordinary-nouns-generally-does","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"The conceptual form of ordinary nouns generally does not possess the syntactic function of <location>.","ja":"普通名詞の概念形は一般に〈場所〉の統語的機能を持たない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0096-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--the-concept-form-of-a-common-noun-can","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"The concept form of a common noun can form a noun phrase by itself and thus has an arity of -1, whereas the affiliative form requires an antecedent and thus has an arity of 0.","ja":"普通名詞の概念形はそれ単独で名詞句を構成できるためアリティは -1 であるのに対し、所属形は先行詞を要求するためアリティは 0 である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--general-nouns-can-function-as-sentence-subject-or","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"General nouns can function as sentence subject or object and may be followed by case postpositions.","ja":"普通名詞は文の主語または目的語になり得、格後置詞の後続を受けることができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--general-nouns-may-be-preceded-by-adnouns-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"General nouns may be preceded by adnouns and adnominalized sentences, and some may take noun suffixes and/or noun prefixes.","ja":"普通名詞は連体詞や連体節の先行を受けることができ、一部は名詞接尾辞や名詞接頭辞を取り得る。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
