{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--nouns-are-classified-on-morphosyntactic-grounds-into-three","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Nouns are classified on morphosyntactic grounds into three major subclasses: common nouns, relational nouns, and bound nouns.","ja":"名詞はその形態統語的性質に基づき、普通名詞、位置名詞（関係名詞）、所属名詞（不完全名詞）の3大下位類に分類される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0007-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--ainu-has-a-nominal-classification-distinguishing-ordinary-nouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu has a nominal classification distinguishing ordinary nouns from locative nouns.","ja":"アイヌ語には普通名詞と位置名詞を区別する名詞分類が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0002-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
