{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--for-animals-sexes-are-distinguished-by-prefixing-pinne","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"For animals, sexes are distinguished by prefixing pinne for male and matne for female.","ja":"動物にあっては、男性（雄）にpinne、女性（雌）にmatneを冠して区別する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["for animals"]},"forms":["pinne","matne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0043-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--just-as-the-noun-ainu-means-human-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Just as the noun ainu means 'human' in contrast to kamui ('god') but 'man' in contrast to menoko ('woman'), the element -kur means 'male' in contrast to -mat.","ja":"ainuという語がkamuiに対して「人」を意味しmenokoに対して「男」を意味するのと同様に、-kurも-matに対しては「男性」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-kur","-mat"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0064-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--in-hidaka-the-words-for-male-spider-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"In Hidaka, the words for male spider and female spider are ka-erikin-kur and ka-erikin-mat, respectively.","ja":"日高方言では、雄蜘蛛と雌蜘蛛をそれぞれ ka-erikin-kur、ka-erikin-mat という。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/mukawa","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ka-erikin-kur","ka-erikin-mat"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0064-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--nouns-placed-after-other-nouns-to-qualify-them","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Nouns placed after other nouns to qualify them, often expressing an indefinite plural, are called adnominal post-words (連体後詞) and are also used as independent nouns.","ja":"名詞に後置して名詞に何らかの限定を加え、不定複数を表す場合が多い語を連体後詞と呼び、これらは独立した名詞としても使われる。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subcategories-of-nouns-can-be-identified-through","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Four subcategories of nouns can be identified through five morphological and syntactic features: inflection, possessive case person affixes, independence, possible modifiers, and locativity.","ja":"名詞の4つの下位区分（普通名詞、位置名詞、代名詞、形式名詞）は、語形変化、所属格人称接辞、自立性、可能な修飾語、場所性の5つの形態・統語的特徴によって識別できる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0092-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--ainu-nouns-are-classified-morphologically-and-affixally-into","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu nouns are classified morphologically and affixally into common nouns, locative/relational nouns, pronouns, and formal nouns.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞は概念形と所属形などの形態論的な区別や人称接辞のとりかたから、普通名詞、位置名詞、代名詞、形式名詞に分けられる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--common-nouns-long-forms-of-positional-nouns-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Common nouns, long forms of positional nouns, and pronouns can independently serve as the subject or object of a verb.","ja":"普通名詞、位置名詞の長形、代名詞は単独で動詞の主語・目的語になることができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0211-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--karafuto-dialects-distinguish-ordinary-nouns-from-locative-nouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--four-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Karafuto dialects distinguish ordinary nouns from locative nouns, and many nouns in both classes have both a non-specific conceptual form and a specific, concrete affiliative form.","ja":"樺太方言では普通名詞と位置名詞が区別され、両クラスの多くの名詞に非特定的な概念形と特定的・具象的な所属形の両方が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0057-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--some-kinship-terms-such-as-unu-hu-his","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--kinship-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Some kinship terms, such as unu-hu 'his mother', ona-ha 'his father', po-ho 'child/son', and sa-ha 'his elder sister', are encoded as inalienable nouns.","ja":"unu-hu「彼の母」、ona-ha「彼の父」、po-ho「子／息子」、sa-ha「彼の姉」などの一部の親族名称は譲渡不能名詞として扱われる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["unu-hu","ona-ha","po-ho","sa-ha","yup-ihi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--kinship-terms-such-as-totto-mother-hapo-father","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--kinship-subclasses"],"statement":{"en":"Kinship terms such as totto 'mother', hapo 'father/mother', acapo 'uncle', unarpe 'aunt', huci 'grandmother', and ekasi 'grandfather' are encoded as alienably possessed nouns.","ja":"totto「母」、hapo「父／母」、acapo「叔父」、unarpe「叔母」、huci「祖母」、ekasi「祖父」などの親族名称は譲渡可能所有名詞として記号化される。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["totto","hapo","acapo","unarpe","huci","ekasi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0006-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns-in-ainu-have-a-basic-form","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Locative nouns in Ainu have a basic form and long forms.","ja":"アイヌ語の位置名詞には基本形と長形がある。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0096-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns-are-always-treated-syntactically-as-location","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Locative nouns are always treated syntactically as <location>.","ja":"位置名詞は統語的に常に〈場所〉として扱われる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0096-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locational-nouns-express-relative-spatial-relations-like-above","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Locational nouns express relative spatial relations like 'above', 'below', 'front', or 'back', and are distinguished grammatically from common nouns by four properties: requiring a preceding reference noun in the basic form, forming long forms differently from affiliative forms, taking objective personal affixes, and always functioning as locations.","ja":"位置名詞は「上」「下」「前」「後」などの相対的位置関係を表し、短形では単独で名詞句になれず基準名詞を要求すること、所属形とは異なる方法で長形を作ること、目的格人称接辞を取れること、文法的に常に〈場所〉として扱われることの4つの特徴で普通名詞と区別される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0235-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--the-basic-form-short-form-of-a-locational","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"The basic form (short form) of a locational noun cannot form a noun phrase or sentence element on its own without a preceding noun that specifies its reference point.","ja":"位置名詞の基本形（短形）は、基準点を示す先行名詞がなければ単独で名詞句をつくることも文の要素になることもできない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":["for basic forms of locational nouns"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0236-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-nouns-are-divided-into-category-1-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-types"],"statement":{"en":"Locative nouns are divided into category 1 and category 2 based on whether or not their basic forms require an antecedent noun phrase.","ja":"位置名詞は基本形が先行名詞句を要求するかどうかに応じて、カテゴリー1位置名詞とカテゴリー2位置名詞に区分される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0096-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locational-nouns-are-divided-into-type-1-locational","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-types"],"statement":{"en":"Locational nouns are divided into Type 1 locational nouns, which cannot stand independently at sentence initial in their basic form, and Type 2 locational nouns, which can.","ja":"位置名詞は、基本形で単独で文頭に立てない第一種位置名詞と、基本形で自立語として文頭に立てる第二種位置名詞に区分される。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0238-04","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--type-1-locative-nouns-have-an-arity-of","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-types"],"statement":{"en":"Type 1 locative nouns have an arity of 0 when preceded by an antecedent, and an arity of -1 when occurring without an antecedent in their long form.","ja":"第一種位置名詞は、先行詞があればアリティは 0 であり、先行詞が無ければ長形で -1 となる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ka","tum","tom"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--type-2-locative-nouns-have-an-arity-of","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--locative-types"],"statement":{"en":"Type 2 locative nouns have an arity of 0 when an antecedent is present, and an arity of -1 when no antecedent is present.","ja":"第二種位置名詞は、先行詞があればアリティは 0 であり、先行詞が無ければ -1 となる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["soy","rik","wor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--pronouns-and-formal-nouns-do-not-show-inflectional","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--pronouns-formals-overview"],"statement":{"en":"Pronouns and formal nouns do not show inflectional changes in form.","ja":"代名詞と形式名詞にはこのような語形変化が見られない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0092-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--pronouns-other-than-personal-pronouns-formal-nouns-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--pronouns-formals-overview"],"statement":{"en":"Pronouns other than personal pronouns, formal nouns, and bound nominal roots each have an arity of -1.","ja":"人称代名詞以外の代名詞、形式名詞、名詞語根はいずれもアリティが -1 である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nep","tanpe","sinep","hi","p","pe","uske","me-","nu-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--in-hokkaido-dialects-proper-nouns-do-not-take","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido dialects, proper nouns do not take affiliative forms, whereas in Sakhalin dialects people's names possess affiliative forms.","ja":"北海道方言では固有名詞は所属形を持たないが、樺太方言では人名が所属形を持つ。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0093-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--in-ainu-there-is-no-grammatical-distinction-between","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, there is no grammatical distinction between proper nouns and common nouns.","ja":"アイヌ語は、英語などと異なり、普通名詞と固有名詞との間に文法的な差は無い。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0230-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--to-avoid-sharing-names-with-others-ainu-personal","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"To avoid sharing names with others, Ainu personal names tended to be long, and most recorded Ainu names consist of two or more words, such as subject + verb or verb + noun.","ja":"似た名前になることを避けるためにアイヌ語の人名は必然的に長くなる傾向があり、記録されているアイヌ語の名前の多くは主語＋動詞、動詞＋名詞のように2語以上で成り立っているものが多い。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["Ekasiwakka","Kinarapuk"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0231-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--in-ainu-nicknames-are-called-pon-re-literally","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, nicknames are called pon re, literally 'little name'.","ja":"アイヌ語であだ名は「小さな名」を意味する pon re と呼ばれる。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pon re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0233-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--names-of-beings-like-okikurmi-or-samayunkur-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Names of beings like Okikurmi or Samayunkur in Hokkaido, and Yayresuupo or Paarionnay in Sakhalin, are considered proper nouns because each denotes a unique individual.","ja":"北海道の Okikurmi や Samayunkur、樺太の Yayresuupo や Paarionnay などの人文神の名は、唯一の個体を指すため固有名詞の範疇に入れられる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["Okikurmi","Samayunkur","Yayresuupo","Paarionnay"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0234-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--in-western-hokkaido-heroic-epics-the-protagonist-poyyaunpe","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"In western Hokkaido heroic epics, the protagonist Poyyaunpe is an epithet meaning 'young land person' that corresponds to a nickname (pon re) and can be treated as a proper noun.","ja":"北海道西部の英雄叙事詩の主人公 Poyyaunpe は「若い陸のやつ」という意味のあだ名（pon re）にあたるものであり、固有名詞として扱ってよい。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["in heroic epics"]},"forms":["Poyyaunpe","pon re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0234-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--expressions-with-the-structure-place-name-un-kur","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Expressions with the structure 'place name + un + kur/mat' such as Iyoci un kur or Kanesanta un mat function within narratives as proper names denoting specific individuals rather than regional groups.","ja":"Iyoci un kur や Kanesanta un mat のような「地名 + un + kur/mat」という語構成の呼称は、物語中では集団ではなく特定の個人を指すため、叙事詩中という限定で固有名詞と見なすことができる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["within epic and narrative discourse"]},"forms":["Iyoci un kur","Kanesanta un mat","un","kur","mat"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0234-03","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-names-can-take-no-prefixes-or-suffixes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Proper names can take no prefixes or suffixes.","ja":"固有名詞は接頭辞も接尾辞も取ることができない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-names-behave-syntactically-like-general-nouns-but","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns","topic:nominal/nominal-subclasses-and-bound-nouns--proper-nouns"],"statement":{"en":"Proper names behave syntactically like general nouns, but unlike general nouns they never take plural suffixes.","ja":"固有名詞は統語的には一般名詞と全く同様に振る舞うが、一般名詞と異なり複数接尾辞をとることは決してない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0082-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
